Package: shunt
Version: @VER@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Boris Kaganovich <bkaganovich@gmail.com>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-fastapi, python3-uvicorn (>= 0.23.1), python3-pydantic, python3-multipart, iproute2, iptables, curl, ca-certificates, procps
Recommends: shunt-xray, sing-box, dnsmasq-base
Suggests: adguardvpn-cli, fptn-client
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Description: Transparent split-routing gateway for a home network
 Shunt routes traffic by destination: domestic traffic goes out directly,
 foreign traffic through a tunnel. Nothing has to be installed on the devices
 behind it, so televisions, consoles and guest hardware are covered too.
 .
 It sits either between the ISP and the router or inside the router's LAN, and
 combines xray-core in TPROXY mode, sing-box, dnsmasq and a DNS-over-HTTPS
 proxy under one web interface on port 80, in Russian or English.
 .
 This package carries the application, its helper scripts and systemd units.
 The xray-core binary lives in shunt-xray; the geoip/geosite rule sets are
 downloaded after installation and refreshed by a weekly timer.
